      "writtenOn": "2019-03-05T22:06:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Like the previous patch: selectable Kconfig options should describe user-visible features, not implementations or internal APIs.  Perhaps this should just be controlled by CONFIG_BLK_INLINE_ENCRYPTION?  Is inline encryption support useful without this?\n\nAlternatively, it could have no prompt string (so it\u0027s not shown to users and can\u0027t be set directly) and be selected by filesystems that need it.",
